                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To determine the correct answer, let's analyze each option:\n\nA) Closing the sails quickly: This action would slow down the boat, but it doesn't necessarily help the sailor navigate to the shore. It might be a part of the process, but it's not the main action needed for navigation.\n\nB) Setting out to sea: This option is the opposite of what the sailor wants to do. They want to navigate to the shore, not go further out to sea.\n\nC) Making an adjustment to the rudder: The rudder is a crucial part of steering a boat. By adjusting the rudder, the sailor can change the direction of the boat and navigate towards the shore. This option seems like the most logical choice for helping the sailor reach their destination.\n\nD) Taking the afternoon off: This option doesn't help the sailor navigate to the shore at all. In fact, it would likely delay their progress.\n\nBased on this analysis, the correct answer is:\n\nC) Making an adjustment to the rudder",
