                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "First, let's rephrase the question: What action should a sailor take to navigate towards the shore?\n\nNow, let's work this out step by step:\n\nA) Closing the sails quickly: This action would slow down the boat, but it doesn't necessarily help in navigating towards the shore.\n\nB) Setting out to sea: This action would take the sailor further away from the shore, so it's not the correct choice.\n\nC) Making an adjustment to the rudder: Adjusting the rudder would change the direction of the boat, which could help the sailor navigate towards the shore.\n\nD) Taking the afternoon off: This action would not help the sailor navigate towards the shore at all.\n\nBased on our reasoning, the correct answer is C) making an adjustment to the rudder.",
