                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To answer this question, let's first understand what respiration is. Respiration is the process by which living organisms take in oxygen and release carbon dioxide. This process is essential for the production of energy required for various life processes.\n\nNow, let's analyze each option:\n\nA) Happens for some species: This statement is not entirely accurate, as respiration is a fundamental process for all living organisms, not just some species.\n\nB) Happens for only land dwelling mammals: This statement is incorrect, as respiration is not limited to land-dwelling mammals. It occurs in all animals, including aquatic animals and invertebrates.\n\nC) Occurs for only sea creatures: This statement is also incorrect, as respiration is not exclusive to sea creatures. As mentioned earlier, it is a process that occurs in all animals, regardless of their habitat.\n\nD) Commonality among all animals: This statement is correct. Respiration is a common process among all animals, as it is essential for their survival and energy production.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is:\n\nD) Commonality among all animals",
