                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "First, let's rephrase the question to ensure we understand it correctly: Which of the following statements best describes respiration?\n\nNow, let's work this out step by step by spelling out our thoughts and reasoning:\n\nA) Respiration happens for some species: This statement is true, but it might not be the best description of respiration since it doesn't specify which species or how common it is.\n\nB) Respiration happens for only land-dwelling mammals: This statement is too specific and excludes many other animals that also undergo respiration, such as birds, fish, and insects.\n\nC) Respiration occurs for only sea creatures: This statement is also too specific and excludes all the land-dwelling animals that undergo respiration.\n\nD) Respiration is a commonality among all animals: This statement is the most accurate description of respiration. All animals, whether they live on land or in water, need to exchange gases with their environment to survive. This process is called respiration.\n\nSo, the right answer is:\nD) Respiration is a commonality among all animals.",
