                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Respiration is a process that is essential for the survival of living organisms. It is the process by which organisms exchange gases, primarily oxygen and carbon dioxide, with their environment. Oxygen is required for cellular respiration, which is the process by which cells produce energy in the form of ATP (adenosine triphosphate). Carbon dioxide is a waste product of cellular respiration and must be removed from the body.\n\nTo determine which option best describes respiration, let's generate sub-questions and answer them:\n\n1. Do only land-dwelling mammals respire?\nNo, respiration is not limited to land-dwelling mammals. Birds, reptiles, amphibians, and even insects also respire.\n\n2. Do only sea creatures respire?\nNo, respiration is not limited to sea creatures. As mentioned earlier, land-dwelling animals also respire.\n\n3. Is respiration a process that occurs in some species only?\nNo, respiration is a fundamental process that occurs in all living organisms, including plants, fungi, and microorganisms.\n\n4. Is respiration a commonality among all animals?\nYes, respiration is a commonality among all animals. All animals require oxygen for cellular respiration and need to eliminate carbon dioxide as a waste product.\n\nBased on the answers to the sub-questions, the correct answer is:\n\nRespiration is a\nD) commonality among all animals.",
                        "answers": [
