                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Professor, I'm having trouble understanding respiration. Can you help me figure out which of these options is correct?\n\nProfessor: Of course! Let's go through each option and see if it makes sense. First, option A says that respiration happens for some species. What do you think about that?\n\nStudent: Well, I know that respiration is the process of taking in oxygen and releasing carbon dioxide, so I think it would apply to more than just some species.\n\nProfessor: That's correct! Now, let's look at option B, which says that respiration happens for only land dwelling mammals. What are your thoughts on that?\n\nStudent: I think that's too specific. I know that fish and birds also respire, so it can't be just for land dwelling mammals.\n\nProfessor: Excellent! You're right, respiration is not limited to land dwelling mammals. Now, let's consider option C, which states that respiration occurs for only sea creatures. What do you think about that?\n\nStudent: That doesn't seem right either. Like I mentioned earlier, I know that birds and land mammals also respire, so it can't be just for sea creatures.\n\nProfessor: You're on a roll! So, that leaves us with option D, which says that respiration is a commonality among all animals. What do you think about that?\n\nStudent: That seems to make the most sense, since we've ruled out the other options. So, respiration is something that all animals have in common?\n\nProfessor: Exactly! You've got it. Respiration is a process that all animals share, as they all need to take in oxygen and release carbon dioxide to survive. Well done!",
