                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step 1: Understand the question. The question is asking about objects that are used to hold sheets of paper together.\n\nStep 2: Analyze the given options. We have four options to choose from: large, wooden, ferromagnetic, and electronic.\n\nStep 3: Think about common objects that hold sheets of paper together. Some examples include paper clips, staples, and binder clips.\n\nStep 4: Compare the common objects to the given options. \n\n- Large: While some objects like binder clips can be large, not all objects that hold sheets of paper together are large. So, this option is not the best choice.\n- Wooden: None of the common objects mentioned above are typically made of wood. So, this option is not correct.\n- Ferromagnetic: Paper clips, staples, and binder clips are all made of metal and can be attracted to magnets. This means they are ferromagnetic. So, this option seems like the best choice.\n- Electronic: None of the common objects mentioned above are electronic. So, this option is not correct.\n\nStep 5: Choose the best option based on the analysis. The best choice is C) ferromagnetic.\n\nAnswer: C) ferromagnetic",
