                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To determine what can be used as a reflector when running at night, we need to consider the properties of each option and how they relate to visibility and reflection.\n\nHelpful knowledge and important additional facts:\n- A reflector is a material or object that reflects light, making it more visible in low-light conditions.\n- When running at night, it's important to wear clothing or accessories that increase visibility to ensure safety.\n\nSub-questions:\n1) Does a black shirt reflect light well?\n2) Does kitchen foil reflect light well?\n3) Do sunglasses reflect light well?\n4) Does a megaphone reflect light well?\n\n1) A black shirt does not reflect light well. Black absorbs light, making it a poor choice for visibility when running at night.\n\n2) Kitchen foil reflects light well. It is made of a shiny, metallic material that bounces light off its surface, making it more visible in low-light conditions.\n\n3) Sunglasses do not reflect light well. They are designed to block and absorb light to protect the eyes, making them a poor choice for visibility when running at night.\n\n4) A megaphone does not reflect light well. It is typically made of plastic and is designed to amplify sound, not reflect light.\n\nBased on the answers to the sub-questions, the best option to use as a reflector when running at night is B) Kitchen foil.",
