                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Professor, I have a question. If I want to go running at night, what can I use as a reflector? Is it A) A black shirt, B) Kitchen foil, C) Sunglasses, or D) A megaphone?\n\nProfessor: Good question! Let's think about the purpose of a reflector. What do you think a reflector should do?\n\nStudent: I think a reflector should make me more visible to others, especially drivers, by reflecting light.\n\nProfessor: Exactly! So, let's go through the options one by one. A black shirt - do you think it would reflect light well?\n\nStudent: No, I think black would absorb light instead of reflecting it.\n\nProfessor: Correct! Now, what about kitchen foil? Do you think it would reflect light?\n\nStudent: Yes, I think kitchen foil is shiny and would reflect light.\n\nProfessor: That's right! Kitchen foil is a good reflector. Now, let's consider sunglasses. Would they be a good reflector for running at night?\n\nStudent: No, I think sunglasses are meant to block light, not reflect it.\n\nProfessor: Correct again! Finally, what about a megaphone? Would it be a good reflector?\n\nStudent: No, I think a megaphone is used for amplifying sound, not reflecting light.\n\nProfessor: Well done! So, based on our discussion, which option do you think is the best reflector for running at night?\n\nStudent: I think the best option is B) Kitchen foil.\n\nProfessor: That's correct! Kitchen foil would be the best reflector among these options. Just make sure to attach it securely to your clothing or gear so it doesn't fall off while you're running.",
