                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Understand the concept of echolocation\nEcholocation is a biological sonar system used by some animals, such as bats and dolphins, to navigate and locate objects in their environment. It works by emitting high-frequency sound waves and then listening to the echoes that bounce back from objects in the environment.\n\nStep 2: Analyze the options\nThe question asks which of the following cannot be detected by echolocation. The options are:\nA) distance\nB) shape\nC) size\nD) temperature\n\nStep 3: Eliminate the options that can be detected by echolocation\nEcholocation is known to be able to detect the distance, shape, and size of objects. Bats, for example, use echolocation to navigate through dark caves and locate insects to eat. They can detect the distance of objects by measuring the time it takes for the sound waves to bounce back to them. They can also detect the shape and size of objects by analyzing the echoes that bounce back.\n\nStep 4: Identify the option that cannot be detected by echolocation\nThe only option left is D) temperature. Echolocation is not capable of detecting the temperature of objects in the environment. This is because temperature is not a property that affects the reflection of sound waves.\n\nStep 5: Conclusion\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) temperature. Echolocation can detect the distance, shape, and size of objects, but it cannot detect their temperature.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "f1f2d7c2-35a6-47d0-a104-b9a4a68a9255",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "D) temperature.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
