                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: What is echolocation?\nEcholocation is a biological sonar system used by some animals, such as bats and dolphins, to navigate and locate prey or obstacles by emitting high-pitched sounds and listening for the echoes that bounce back.\n\nStep 2: What information can echolocation detect?\nEcholocation can detect the distance, shape, and size of objects by analyzing the time delay, frequency, and intensity of the echoes. However, echolocation cannot detect the temperature of objects.\n\nStep 3: Which option matches the information that echolocation cannot detect?\nThe correct answer is D) temperature.",
