                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step 1: Understand what echolocation is.\nEcholocation is a method used by some animals, like bats and dolphins, to determine the location and features of objects in their environment by emitting sounds and listening to the echoes that return.\n\nStep 2: Analyze each option.\n\nA) Distance - Echolocation can detect an object's distance because the time it takes for the emitted sound to return as an echo can be used to calculate how far away the object is.\n\nB) Shape - Echolocation can detect an object's shape because the way the sound waves bounce off the object and return as echoes can provide information about the object's contours and structure.\n\nC) Size - Echolocation can detect an object's size because the intensity and pattern of the returning echoes can give clues about the object's dimensions.\n\nD) Temperature - Echolocation relies on sound waves, which are not directly affected by an object's temperature. Therefore, echolocation cannot detect an object's temperature.\n\nStep 3: Choose the correct answer.\nThe correct answer is D) temperature.",
