                    {
                        "id": "9243d4bc-5649-4e96-92d6-407bd471bafb",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-12",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To answer this question, let's first understand what echolocation is and how it works. Echolocation is a method used by some animals, such as bats and dolphins, to determine the location and characteristics of objects in their environment. They do this by emitting sounds and then listening for the echoes that bounce back from objects. By analyzing the time it takes for the echoes to return and the characteristics of the echoes, the animals can determine various aspects of the objects.\n\nNow let's go through each of the options and see which one echolocation can't detect:\n\nA) Distance: Echolocation can detect the distance of an object. The time it takes for the emitted sound to bounce back and return to the animal can be used to calculate the distance to the object. The longer it takes for the echo to return, the farther away the object is.\n\nB) Shape: Echolocation can also detect the shape of an object. The characteristics of the echoes, such as their intensity and frequency, can provide information about the object's shape. For example, a smooth, flat surface will reflect sound differently than a rough, irregular surface.\n\nC) Size: Echolocation can determine the size of an object as well. The intensity of the echoes can provide information about the size of the object. Larger objects will generally produce stronger echoes, while smaller objects will produce weaker echoes.\n\nD) Temperature: Echolocation does not provide information about an object's temperature. The sound waves used in echolocation are not sensitive to temperature differences, and the echoes do not carry information about the temperature of the object.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) temperature. Echolocation can't detect an object's temperature.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "51dcfa91-ac85-4904-9b50-65e3be9c7d83",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "D) temperature.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
                        "author": "thoughtsource",
                        "date": "2023/04/13 04:02:35",
                        "api_service": "openai_chat",
