                    },
                    {
                        "id": "bb27cdab-9531-429c-b83b-f2a11541494f",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-13",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "First, let's rephrase the question to ensure we understand it correctly: Which of the following cannot be detected by echolocation?\n\nNow, let's work this out step by step by spelling out our thoughts and reasoning:\n\nEcholocation is a method used by animals like bats and dolphins to navigate and locate objects by emitting sounds and listening to the echoes that return from objects in their environment. By analyzing the time delay and frequency of the returning echoes, they can determine various properties of the objects.\n\nA) Distance: Echolocation can detect the distance of an object because the time it takes for the emitted sound to return as an echo is directly related to the distance of the object.\n\nB) Shape: Echolocation can detect the shape of an object because the returning echoes will have different patterns depending on the shape of the object. For example, a flat surface will reflect sound differently than a curved one.\n\nC) Size: Echolocation can detect the size of an object because larger objects will reflect more sound waves, resulting in a stronger echo. Additionally, the pattern of the returning echoes can provide information about the size of the object.\n\nD) Temperature: Echolocation relies on sound waves, which are not directly affected by the temperature of an object. While temperature can affect the speed of sound in the surrounding medium (e.g., air or water), it does not provide information about the temperature of the object itself.\n\nBased on our reasoning, the correct answer is:\n\nD) Temperature - Echolocation cannot detect an object's temperature.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "da400dba-3f0c-4c17-a6c4-72c607277044",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "D) Temperature. Echolocation cannot detect an object's temperature.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
                        "author": "thoughtsource",
                        "date": "2023/04/13 04:03:21",
                        "api_service": "openai_chat",
