                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nStep 1: Understand what echolocation is.\nEcholocation is a biological sonar used by some animals to detect objects in their environment. It works by emitting sound waves and then listening for the echoes that bounce off of objects in the environment.\n\nStep 2: Understand what each of the answer choices mean.\nA) Distance: the amount of space between two points.\nB) Shape: the form or outline of an object.\nC) Size: the dimensions of an object.\nD) Temperature: a measure of how hot or cold something is.\n\nStep 3: Determine which answer choice is correct.\nEcholocation can detect an object's distance, shape, and size, but not its temperature. Therefore, the correct answer is D) Temperature.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "4d5d5468-a05e-48c7-9bd2-e14feeacba63",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
