                        "cot": "Plan:\n1. Determine the number of pages in the calendar.\n2. Multiply the number of pages by 2 since each page represents one month.\n3. Subtract 2 from the result since the first and last pages are only changed once.\n4. The final result will be the number of times someone would change the page of a calendar in a year.\n\nAnswer:\n1. Most calendars have 12 pages, one for each month.\n2. 12 x 2 = 24\n3. 24 - 2 = 22\n4. The answer is D) 14.",
