                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Question: How many times would a person need to turn the page of a calendar in a year?\n\nLet's work this out step by step:\n\n1. A calendar typically has one page for each month, and there are 12 months in a year.\n2. To change the page, a person would need to turn the page at the end of each month.\n3. Since there are 12 months, the person would need to turn the page 12 times.\n4. However, we also need to consider the first time the person turns the page from the cover to the first month, which adds one more page turn.\n\nSo, the total number of times a person would need to change the page of a calendar in a year is 12 (for each month) + 1 (for the initial turn from the cover) = 13.\n\nThe correct answer is A) 13.",
