                        "cot": "\nStudent: How many times would someone change the page of a calendar in a year?\n\nProfessor: That's a great question. Let's break it down. A calendar year is 365 days long, and most calendars are divided into 12 months. So, if you divide 365 days by 12 months, you get 30.4 days per month. That means that you would need to change the page of the calendar every 30 days, or 12 times in a year. So the answer is B) 12. Does that make sense?",
