                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nStep 1: Understand the definition of photosynthesis. Photosynthesis is the process by which plants use light energy to convert carbon dioxide and water into glucose and oxygen.\n\nStep 2: Identify the ingredients necessary for photosynthesis. Photosynthesis requires carbon dioxide (CO2), water (H20), and sunlight.\n\nStep 3: Eliminate the incorrect answers. Answer A is incorrect because argon is not necessary for photosynthesis. Answer B is incorrect because fertilizer is not necessary for photosynthesis. Answer C is incorrect because cloudy skies are not necessary for photosynthesis.\n\nAnswer: D) CO2, H20, and sun rays",
                        "answers": [
