                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Question: Which statement correctly describes carnivores?\nA) They exclusively consume foliage and vegetables\nB) They are at the bottom of the food chain\nC) They need prey to survive\nD) They need carbon dioxide to survive\n\nStep 1: Analyze each statement to determine if it accurately describes carnivores.\n\nA) Carnivores are animals that primarily eat other animals, so they do not exclusively consume foliage and vegetables. This statement is incorrect.\n\nB) Carnivores are typically higher up on the food chain because they consume other animals. They are not at the bottom of the food chain. This statement is incorrect.\n\nC) Carnivores rely on consuming other animals (prey) for their survival, as they obtain their energy and nutrients from these sources. This statement is correct.\n\nD) While all living organisms require some level of carbon dioxide for various biological processes, it is not a primary requirement for carnivores to survive. This statement is incorrect.\n\nStep 2: Identify the correct statement.\n\nBased on our analysis, statement C (Carnivores require prey to survive) is the correct description of carnivores.",
