                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The question is asking about the sources of pollen and seeds. Pollen and seeds are both reproductive structures found in plants. Pollen is a fine powdery substance containing microscopic grains discharged from the male part of a flower, while seeds are the mature fertilized ovule of a plant, containing an embryo and capable of germinating to produce a new plant.\n\nNow, let's analyze the given options:\n\nA) Lakes that are frozen over: Lakes are bodies of water and do not produce pollen or seeds. This option is incorrect.\n\nB) Things you give a loved one in a bouquet: A bouquet typically consists of flowers, which are the reproductive structures of plants. Flowers produce pollen and can develop into fruits containing seeds. This option seems to be correct.\n\nC) Various types of animals: Animals do not produce pollen or seeds, as they reproduce through different mechanisms, such as producing eggs or giving birth to live offspring. This option is incorrect.\n\nD) A person that is healthy: Humans, like animals, do not produce pollen or seeds. This option is incorrect.\n\nAnswer: B) Things you give a loved one in a bouquet, which are flowers, produce pollen and seeds.",
