                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step 1: Understand the question - The question is asking whether the Qwerty keyboard layout was created before computers existed.\n\nStep 2: Research the history of the Qwerty keyboard layout - Look up information on when the Qwerty keyboard layout was invented and by whom.\n\nStep 3: Research the history of computers - Look up information on when computers were invented and what the first computers looked like.\n\nStep 4: Compare the dates - Compare the date of the invention of the Qwerty keyboard layout to the date of the invention of computers.\n\nStep 5: Determine the answer - Based on the comparison of the dates, determine whether the Qwerty keyboard layout predates computers or not.\n\nAnswer: After researching, it is found that the Qwerty keyboard layout was created in 1873 by Christopher Latham Sholes, an American newspaper editor and printer. The first computers, such as the ENIAC, were invented in the 1940s. Therefore, the Qwerty keyboard layout predates computers.\n\nA) True",
