                    {
                        "id": "5aa7766d-5702-41c1-b7ff-b91f03c99344",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-12",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To answer this question, let's first understand what the Qwerty keyboard layout is and when it was invented.\n\nThe Qwerty keyboard layout is the most widely used keyboard layout in the world. It was created by Christopher Latham Sholes, an American newspaper editor and printer, in the 1860s. The name \"Qwerty\" comes from the first six letters in the top row of the keyboard.\n\nNow, let's consider the invention of computers. The first electronic digital computer, called the Electronic Numerical Integrator and Computer (ENIAC), was invented in 1945. However, the concept of a computer dates back to the 19th century with the invention of the Analytical Engine by Charles Babbage in the 1830s.\n\nSince the Qwerty keyboard layout was invented in the 1860s, and the concept of a computer dates back to the 1830s, it might seem that the Qwerty keyboard layout did not predate computers. However, the first electronic digital computer was not invented until 1945, which is much later than the invention of the Qwerty keyboard layout.\n\nTherefore, the answer is:\n\nA) True\n\nThe Qwerty keyboard layout predates electronic digital computers.",
