                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Question: Did the Qwerty keyboard layout exist before computers?\nA) True\nB) False\n\nTo answer this question, let's first understand what the Qwerty keyboard layout is and when it was invented. The Qwerty keyboard layout is the most common keyboard layout used today, with the first six letters on the top row being Q, W, E, R, T, and Y. It was created by Christopher Latham Sholes, an American newspaper editor and printer, in the 1860s.\n\nNow, let's consider the history of computers. The first electronic digital computer, called the Electronic Numerical Integrator and Computer (ENIAC), was invented in 1945. However, the concept of a computer dates back to the 19th century with Charles Babbage's Analytical Engine, which was a mechanical computer.\n\nSince the Qwerty keyboard layout was created in the 1860s and the concept of a computer dates back to the 19th century, it is possible that the Qwerty keyboard layout predates computers. However, the first electronic digital computer was not invented until 1945, which is after the invention of the Qwerty keyboard layout.\n\nTherefore, the answer is:\nA) True",
                        "answers": [
