                        "cot": "Student: Professor, I don't understand the question. Who is Jason and what does he have to do with polo?\n\nProfessor: Jason is a character from Greek mythology who led the Argonauts on a quest for the Golden Fleece. Polo is a sport played on horseback with teams of four players.\n\nStudent: Okay, but how does that relate to the question?\n\nProfessor: The question is asking if the children of Jason, if he had any, could hypothetically fill a polo team. In other words, could there be enough of them to make up a team of four players?\n\nStudent: Oh, I see. So, do we know if Jason had any children?\n\nProfessor: Yes, Jason had two children with his wife, Medea. Their names were Mermeros and Pheres.\n\nStudent: And how many players are on a polo team?\n\nProfessor: There are four players on a polo team.\n\nStudent: So, if Jason had two children, could they fill a polo team?\n\nProfessor: No, two children would not be enough to fill a polo team. We need four players, so we would need at least two more children.\n\nStudent: Okay, I understand now. So the answer to the question is false.\n\nProfessor: That's correct. The answer is false.",
