                        "cot": "Student: Can you explain the question a bit more, please?\n\nProfessor: Of course. The question is asking if spiders can be useful in controlling parasites for eggplant farmers.\n\nStudent: Okay, so what kind of parasites are we talking about here?\n\nProfessor: We're talking about pests that can damage eggplants, such as aphids and mites.\n\nStudent: And how would spiders help with that?\n\nProfessor: Spiders are natural predators of these pests. They can eat them and help keep their populations under control.\n\nStudent: So, is the answer true or false?\n\nProfessor: The answer is true. Spiders can be helpful for eggplant farmers in controlling parasites.",
