                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: What are yin and yang colors?\nYin and yang are concepts from Chinese philosophy that represent opposite forces or energies. In terms of colors, yin colors are considered cool and dark, while yang colors are warm and bright. Examples of yin colors include blue, green, and purple, while examples of yang colors include red, orange, and yellow.\n\nStep 2: How are rainbows formed?\nRainbows are formed when sunlight is refracted, or bent, as it passes through water droplets in the air. This causes the light to separate into its component colors, which we see as a rainbow.\n\nStep 3: Do rainbows involve mixing yin and yang colors?\nNo, rainbows do not involve mixing yin and yang colors. Instead, they involve the separation of white light into its component colors through refraction. While some of the colors in a rainbow may be considered yin or yang, the formation of the rainbow itself does not involve mixing these colors.\n\nStep 4: What is the answer to the question?\nThe answer is B) False. Rainbows are not devoid of color made by mixing yin and yang colors.",
                        "answers": [
