                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step 1: Understand the concept of rainbows\nRainbows are a meteorological phenomenon that is caused by reflection, refraction, and dispersion of light in water droplets resulting in a spectrum of light appearing in the sky.\n\nStep 2: Understand the concept of yin and yang colors\nYin and yang are concepts in Chinese philosophy that describe how seemingly opposite or contrary forces may actually be complementary, interconnected, and interdependent. Yin and yang colors typically refer to contrasting colors, such as black and white or dark and light shades.\n\nStep 3: Analyze the connection between rainbows and yin and yang colors\nRainbows are formed by the dispersion of light, which creates a spectrum of colors. These colors are not created by mixing yin and yang colors, but rather by the natural process of light interacting with water droplets in the atmosphere.\n\nConclusion: Rainbows are not devoid of color made by mixing yin and yang colors. So, the answer is B) False.",
