                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Yin and yang are two opposing forces in Chinese philosophy.\n\nStep 2: Yin and yang colors are black and white.\n\nStep 3: A rainbow is made up of seven colors: red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo, and violet.\n\nStep 4: Therefore, a rainbow made up of only yin and yang colors (black and white) would be devoid of color.\n\nAnswer: B) False",
