                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": " \n\nFirst, we need to understand what yin and yang colors are. Yin colors are generally cool colors like blue and green, while yang colors are generally warm colors like red and orange.\n\nNow, let's think about how a rainbow is made. A rainbow is created when sunlight passes through water droplets in the air. The sunlight is then refracted, or bent, and separated into its different colors. So, a rainbow is actually made up of all the colors of the visible spectrum: red, orange, yellow, green, blue, and violet.\n\nNow that we know all of this, we can answer the question. A rainbow is not devoid of color because it is made up of all the colors of the visible spectrum. However, a rainbow could be considered to be made up of both yin and yang colors, since it contains both cool and warm colors.",
