                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step 1: Understand the question\nThe question is asking if a beaver's teeth can be compared to or are as impressive as a Smilodon's teeth.\n\nStep 2: Research about beaver's teeth\nBeavers have sharp, strong teeth that are adapted for gnawing on wood. Their front teeth (incisors) are orange due to the presence of iron, which makes them strong and durable.\n\nStep 3: Research about Smilodon's teeth\nSmilodon, also known as the saber-toothed cat, had long, sharp canine teeth that could grow up to 11 inches in length. These teeth were used for stabbing and slicing through the flesh of their prey.\n\nStep 4: Compare the teeth of both animals\nWhile beavers have strong teeth adapted for gnawing on wood, Smilodon's teeth were much larger and designed for hunting and killing large prey. The size and purpose of their teeth are quite different.\n\nStep 5: Answer the question\nB) False\nA beaver's teeth would not rival that of a Smilodon, as they serve different purposes and have different sizes and structures.",
