                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Question: Do the teeth of a beaver rival those of a Smilodon?\n\nFirst, let's understand the characteristics of both animals' teeth.\n\nBeavers are known for their large, sharp incisors that are used for gnawing on wood. These teeth are constantly growing and are self-sharpening due to the harder enamel on the front and softer dentin on the back.\n\nSmilodon, also known as the saber-toothed cat, was a prehistoric carnivore with long, curved canine teeth that could reach up to 11 inches in length. These teeth were used for stabbing and slicing through the flesh of their prey.\n\nNow, let's compare the teeth of both animals.\n\nBeaver teeth are specialized for gnawing on wood, while Smilodon teeth are specialized for hunting and killing prey. The size, shape, and function of their teeth are quite different.\n\nConsidering these differences, it is clear that the teeth of a beaver do not rival those of a Smilodon.\n\nAnswer: B) False",
                        "answers": [
