                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Professor, I'm having trouble understanding if a beaver's teeth would rival that of a Smilodon. Can you help me work through this question?\n\nProfessor: Of course! Let's start by discussing what we know about each animal's teeth. What do you know about a beaver's teeth?\n\nStudent: Well, I know that beavers have large, sharp front teeth that they use for gnawing on wood.\n\nProfessor: That's correct. Now, what do you know about a Smilodon's teeth?\n\nStudent: Smilodon is also known as the saber-toothed cat, so I assume it has large, sharp teeth as well.\n\nProfessor: Yes, that's right. Smilodon had long, curved canine teeth that were used for stabbing and slicing through the flesh of their prey. Now, let's think about the purpose of each animal's teeth. What is the main function of a beaver's teeth?\n\nStudent: The main function of a beaver's teeth is to cut through wood and strip bark from trees.\n\nProfessor: Correct. And what about the Smilodon's teeth? What was their main function?\n\nStudent: The main function of a Smilodon's teeth was to kill and eat their prey.\n\nProfessor: Exactly. So, considering the different functions of each animal's teeth, do you think a beaver's teeth would rival that of a Smilodon?\n\nStudent: I guess not, since they have different functions and are adapted for different purposes.\n\nProfessor: That's right. So, what would be the correct answer to the question?\n\nStudent: The correct answer would be B) False.\n\nProfessor: Excellent! You've worked through the question and arrived at the correct answer. Do you have any other questions about this topic?\n\nStudent: No, I think I understand it now. Thank you for your help, Professor!",
