                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "No, embalmed bodies do not feel different at funerals. Embalming is a process that preserves the body for viewing and burial, and it does not affect the body's ability to feel. The person who has died is not aware of anything, and there is no reason to believe that they would be able to feel anything during a funeral. Embalmed bodies do not feel different at funerals.",
