                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nFirst, what is embalming? Embalming is the process of preserving a corpse by using chemicals. The most common chemicals used are formaldehyde, glutaraldehyde, and phenol.\n\nSecond, how does this process work? The chemicals are injected into the body through the arteries, and they work to preserve the body by preventing decomposition.\n\nThird, what does this mean for how the body feels? The body will feel stiff and will not decompose.\n\nFourth, how does this affect funerals? The body will look and feel different than it would if it were not",
