                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Embalming is the process of preserving a deceased body through the use of chemicals and other treatments. It is often done to delay decomposition and to make the body presentable for viewing at a funeral.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is the purpose of embalming?\n2. How does embalming affect the physical properties of a body?\n3. Can embalming change the way a body feels to the touch?\n\nAnswering sub-questions:\n1. The purpose of embalming is to delay decomposition and to make the body presentable for viewing at a funeral.\n2. Embalming can change the physical properties of a body by replacing bodily fluids with embalming fluid, which can cause the body to become more rigid and firm.\n3. It is possible that embalming can change the way a body feels to the touch, as the embalming fluid can cause the skin to become more firm and less pliable.\n\nAnswer to original question:\nBased on the information gathered, it is possible that embalmed bodies may feel different at funerals due to the effects of embalming. Therefore, the answer is A) True.",
