                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Question: Is there a significant difference between the appearance of anatomical hearts and symbolic hearts?\n\nStep 1: Define anatomical hearts and symbolic hearts.\nAnatomical hearts refer to the actual organ in the human body responsible for pumping blood. It has a complex structure with chambers, valves, and blood vessels. Symbolic hearts, on the other hand, are the simplified, often symmetrical shape commonly used to represent love and affection. This shape typically consists of two half circles on top and a V-shape at the bottom.\n\nStep 2: Compare the appearances of anatomical hearts and symbolic hearts.\nAnatomical hearts have a more intricate and irregular shape, with various parts such as the atria, ventricles, and blood vessels. Symbolic hearts are a simplified, stylized representation that does not accurately depict the structure of an actual heart.\n\nStep 3: Determine if there is a significant difference between the two.\nGiven the differences in structure and appearance between anatomical hearts and symbolic hearts, it is clear that they look remarkably different.\n\nAnswer: A) True",
