                    {
                        "id": "242719a3-4047-4aaf-9333-0e0d655c002e",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-16",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To answer this question, we need to first understand what anatomical and symbolic hearts are and then compare their appearances.\n\nAnatomical hearts refer to the actual human heart, which is a muscular organ responsible for pumping blood throughout the body. It is roughly the size of a fist and has a complex structure with four chambers, valves, and blood vessels.\n\nSymbolic hearts, on the other hand, are the stylized representations of the heart that are commonly used to symbolize love, affection, and emotions. The symbolic heart shape is often seen on Valentine's Day cards, in emojis, and in various forms of art and design.\n\nNow, let's compare the appearances of anatomical and symbolic hearts:\n\n1. Shape: Anatomical hearts have an irregular, somewhat conical shape, while symbolic hearts have a symmetrical shape with two rounded lobes at the top and a pointed end at the bottom.\n\n2. Chambers and Valves: Anatomical hearts have four chambers (two atria and two ventricles) and multiple valves to regulate blood flow. Symbolic hearts do not depict these internal structures.\n\n3. Blood Vessels: Anatomical hearts have major blood vessels such as the aorta, pulmonary artery, and vena cava connected to them. Symbolic hearts do not show any blood vessels.\n\n4. Size and Proportion: Anatomical hearts are roughly the size of a fist and have a more realistic proportion in terms of size and shape. Symbolic hearts are often depicted in various sizes and proportions, depending on the context and artistic style.\n\nBased on these comparisons, we can conclude that anatomical and symbolic hearts look remarkably different. So, the answer is:\n\nA) True",
                        "answers": [
