                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To answer this question, we need to consider the following facts and sub-questions:\n\n1. Who was the 40th president of the United States?\n2. When was the 40th president in office?\n3. What is a lolcat?\n4. When did lolcats become popular?\n5. Did the 40th president have access to the technology required to forward lolcats?\n\n1. The 40th president of the United States was Ronald Reagan.\n2. Ronald Reagan was in office from January 20, 1981, to January 20, 1989.\n3. A lolcat is an image of a cat with a humorous caption, typically in broken English or internet slang.\n4. Lolcats became popular in the mid-2000s, particularly through the website I Can Has Cheezburger?, which was created in 2007.\n5. During Reagan's presidency, the internet was not widely available to the public, and email was not a common method of communication. The World Wide Web was not invented until 1989, after Reagan left office.\n\nBased on this information, we can conclude that:\n\nB) False - The 40th president of the United States, Ronald Reagan, did not forward lolcats to his friends, as they became popular after his presidency and he did not have access to the technology required to forward them.",
