                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To answer this question, we need to compare the weight of a Toyota Hilux and Mr. Ed, a famous talking horse from a 1960s television show. \n\nHelpful knowledge and important additional facts:\n1. The Toyota Hilux is a pickup truck produced by the Japanese automobile manufacturer Toyota.\n2. Mr. Ed is a fictional talking horse, portrayed by a Palomino horse named Bamboo Harvester.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is the weight of a Toyota Hilux?\n2. What is the weight of Mr. Ed (Bamboo Harvester)?\n\nAnswering sub-questions:\n1. The weight of a Toyota Hilux varies depending on the model and configuration. However, a typical weight range for a Toyota Hilux is between 1,800 kg (3,968 lbs) and 2,200 kg (4,850 lbs).\n2. The weight of a Palomino horse, like Bamboo Harvester, can range from 450 kg (990 lbs) to 1,100 kg (2,425 lbs), depending on the specific breed, age, and size of the horse.\n\nAnswering the original question:\nComparing the weight of a Toyota Hilux (1,800 kg - 2,200 kg) and Mr. Ed (450 kg - 1,100 kg), it is clear that the Toyota Hilux is significantly heavier than Mr. Ed. Therefore, the Toyota Hilux would tip the scales against Mr. Ed.\n\nThe answer is A) True.",
