                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step 1: Research the temperature and weather conditions on Mercury.\nStep 2: Determine what type of clothing would be appropriate for those conditions.\nStep 3: Compare the appropriate clothing to warm weather attire.\nStep 4: Determine if warm weather attire would be a good idea on Mercury based on the comparison.\n\nAfter researching, we find that Mercury has extreme temperature fluctuations, ranging from -290\u00b0F (-180\u00b0C) at night to 800\u00b0F (430\u00b0C) during the day. This means that warm weather attire would not be sufficient to protect against the extreme cold at night, and no clothing would be able to protect against the extreme heat during the day. Therefore, the answer is:\n\nB) False",
