                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "B) False\n\nMercury is the closest planet to the Sun, so one might assume that it is always hot and that warm weather attire would be appropriate. However, Mercury has no atmosphere to retain heat, so the temperature on the planet varies greatly between day and night.\n\nDuring the day, temperatures on Mercury can reach up to 800 degrees Fahrenheit (430 degrees Celsius), which is much hotter than any warm weather attire could handle. At night, temperatures can drop to -290 degrees Fahrenheit (-180 degrees Celsius), which would require extremely cold weather attire.\n\nTherefore, only warm weather attire would not be a good idea on Mercury due to the extreme temperature fluctuations between day and night.",
