                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Question: Is it a good idea to wear only warm weather attire on Mercury?\nA) True\nB) False\n\nTo answer this question, let's consider the conditions on Mercury and how they would affect the suitability of warm weather attire.\n\nMercury is the closest planet to the Sun, so one might assume that it is always hot. However, Mercury has no atmosphere to retain heat, so its temperature varies greatly between day and night. During the day, temperatures can reach up to 800 degrees Fahrenheit (430 degrees Celsius), while at night, temperatures can drop to -290 degrees Fahrenheit (-180 degrees Celsius).\n\nWarm weather attire, such as shorts and t-shirts, would not provide adequate protection against the extreme temperatures on Mercury. During the day, the high temperatures would be too hot for such clothing, and at night, the cold temperatures would require much warmer clothing to stay safe.\n\nTherefore, the answer is:\nB) False",
                        "answers": [
