                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Professor, I'm not sure if only warm weather attire would be a good idea on Mercury. Can you help me understand this better?\n\nProfessor: Of course! Let's start by discussing the temperature conditions on Mercury. Do you know how hot and cold it can get on the planet?\n\nStudent: I think it can get extremely hot during the day and very cold at night, but I'm not sure about the exact temperatures.\n\nProfessor: That's correct. Mercury's temperature can range from about 800 degrees Fahrenheit (430 degrees Celsius) during the day to -290 degrees Fahrenheit (-180 degrees Celsius) at night. Now, considering these extreme temperatures, what do you think about wearing only warm weather attire on Mercury?\n\nStudent: I guess it would be suitable during the day when it's extremely hot, but not at night when it's freezing cold.\n\nProfessor: Exactly. So, based on this information, would you say that only warm weather attire would be a good idea on Mercury?\n\nStudent: No, I think it would be a bad idea since it wouldn't protect you from the extreme cold at night.\n\nProfessor: That's correct! So, the answer to the question is B) False. Only warm weather attire would not be a good idea on Mercury due to the extreme temperature variations.",
