                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Professor, I'm having trouble understanding the concept of a \"light year.\" Can you help me figure out which of these options is the correct definition?\n\nProfessor: Of course! Let's start by breaking down the term \"light year.\" What do you think the word \"light\" refers to in this context?\n\nStudent: I think it refers to the speed of light.\n\nProfessor: That's correct! Now, what about the word \"year\"? What do you think that refers to?\n\nStudent: It refers to the time period of one year.\n\nProfessor: Exactly! So, combining those two ideas, what do you think a \"light year\" might represent?\n\nStudent: I guess it would be the distance that light travels in one year.\n\nProfessor: That's correct! So, looking at the options, which one matches that definition?\n\nStudent: Option A) the distance light travels in one year.\n\nProfessor: Well done! You've worked it out. A \"light year\" is the distance light travels in one year. Do you understand how we got to the right answer?\n\nStudent: Yes, I do. Thank you for helping me work through it step by step, Professor!",
