                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nStudent: What is a light year?\n\nProfessor: A light year is the distance light travels in one year. It is the distance light travels in a vacuum in one year, which is about 9.5 trillion kilometers.\n\nStudent: How is that calculated?\n\nProfessor: The calculation is based on the speed of light, which is 299,792,458 meters per second. So, if you multiply that number by the number of seconds in a year, which is 31,536,000, you get the distance light travels in one year, which is 9.5 trillion kilometers.",
