                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nAnswer: B) Gravity causes gases and dust particles to condense into spheres.\n\nExplanation: Gravity plays an important role in the formation of stars. It is the force that causes the gases and dust particles in a nebula to condense into a sphere, which is the first step in the formation of a star. As the particles become more and more dense, the gravitational force increases, causing the particles to collapse further and further until the core of the sphere becomes hot enough to ignite nuclear fusion. This is the process by which stars are formed. Therefore, the statement that best describes the role of gravity in the formation of stars is B) Gravity causes gases and dust particles to condense into spheres.",
