                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nAnswer: B) Gravity causes gases and dust particles to condense into spheres.\n\nExplanation: Gravity plays a major role in the formation of stars. It is the force that pulls together the gas and dust particles that form the star. As the particles are pulled together, they become denser and denser until they form a sphere. This process is known as gravitational collapse. Therefore, the statement that best describes the role of gravity in the formation of stars is that it causes gases and dust particles to condense into spheres.",
