                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nFirst, we need to understand what the rock cycle is. The rock cycle is a continuous process that describes how rocks are formed, broken down, and transformed into different types of rocks over time. There are three main types of rocks: igneous, sedimentary, and metamorphic.\n\nNow, let's look at the options:\n\nA) Cooling temperatures: This is correct. Igneous rocks form from the cooling and solidification of magma or lava. As the molten rock cools, it solidifies and forms an igneous rock.\n\nB) High pressure and heat: This is more characteristic of metamorphic rocks, which form from the transformation of existing rocks under high pressure and heat.\n\nC) Weathering and erosion: This is more characteristic of sedimentary rocks, which form from the accumulation and cementation of sediment particles that have been weathered and eroded from existing rocks.\n\nD) Compacted plant remains: This is more characteristic of organic sedimentary rocks, such as coal, which form from the accumulation and compaction of plant remains over time.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A) cooling temperatures.",
