                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": " Igneous rocks can either form from solidified lava or magma. Lava is molten rock that is on the Earth's surface. Magma is molten rock that is below the Earth's surface. \n\nWeathering and erosion can break down rocks into smaller pieces, but it cannot create a rock. \n\nCompacted plant remains can create a sedimentary rock, but not an igneous rock. \n\nThat leaves A) cooling temperatures and B) high pressure and heat. Igneous rocks can form when lava or magma cools down. This can happen on the Earth's surface or below the surface. Igneous rocks can also form when magma is under high pressure and heat. \n\nThe correct answer is B) high pressure and heat.",
