                        "instruction": "qa-12",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To answer this question, let's first understand what the rock cycle is and how igneous rocks are formed.\n\nThe rock cycle is a continuous process in which rocks are created, changed, and destroyed through various geological processes. There are three main types of rocks: igneous, sedimentary, and metamorphic. Each type of rock is formed through different processes.\n\nIgneous rocks are formed when molten rock, or magma, cools and solidifies. This can happen either below the Earth's surface (intrusive igneous rocks) or on the Earth's surface (extrusive igneous rocks) when magma is expelled through volcanic eruptions.\n\nNow let's analyze each option:\n\nA) Cooling temperatures: This option is correct. As mentioned earlier, igneous rocks form when magma cools and solidifies. The cooling process allows the minerals in the magma to crystallize and form solid rock.\n\nB) High pressure and heat: This option is incorrect. High pressure and heat are responsible for the formation of metamorphic rocks, not igneous rocks. Metamorphic rocks are formed when existing rocks are subjected to high temperatures and pressures, causing the minerals in the rock to change and recrystallize.\n\nC) Weathering and erosion: This option is incorrect. Weathering and erosion are processes that break down rocks into smaller particles, which can eventually form sedimentary rocks. Sedimentary rocks are formed when these particles accumulate and become compacted and cemented together.\n\nD) Compacted plant remains: This option is incorrect. Compacted plant remains are responsible for the formation of a specific type of sedimentary rock called coal. Coal forms when dead plant material accumulates and becomes compacted over millions of years.\n\nBased on the information above, the correct answer is:\n\nIn the rock cycle, an igneous rock forms from:\nA) cooling temperatures",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "a783c83a-4c66-46f8-84a7-66a9fd153803",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "A) cooling temperatures.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
                        "author": "thoughtsource",
                        "date": "2023/04/13 06:54:46",
