                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nA) cooling temperatures\nB) high pressure and heat\nC) weathering and erosion\nD) compacted plant remains\n\nIgneous rocks form from solidified lava or magma. Lava is molten rock that is expelled from a volcano during an eruption. Magma is molten rock that is found beneath the earth's surface. Igneous rocks can also form from the solidification of lava or magma on the earth's surface.",
