                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nThe correct answer is B) high pressure and heat.\n\nIgneous rocks form when molten rock (magma) cools and solidifies. This process is known as crystallization. Magma is formed when rocks are heated to very high temperatures due to the high pressure and heat found deep within the Earth's crust. As the magma rises to the surface, it cools and solidifies, forming an igneous rock.\n\nA) cooling temperatures is incorrect because cooling temperatures alone are not enough to form an igneous rock.\n\nC) weathering and erosion is incorrect because weathering and erosion are processes that break down rocks, not form them.\n\nD) compacted plant remains is incorrect because compacted plant remains are not hot enough to form an igneous rock.",
