                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nAnswer: A) Rock cools quickly from melted rock.\n\nPlan:\n1. Read the question and the answer choices.\n2. Consider the definition of surface rock formation on volcanoes.\n3. Eliminate answer choices that do not fit the definition.\n4. Consider the remaining answer choices and determine which one best fits the definition.\n\nSurface rock formation on volcanoes is the process of molten rock (magma) cooling and solidifying on the surface of the volcano. This process is known as extrusive igneous rock formation. Therefore, the major process of surface rock formation on volcanoes is A) Rock cools quickly from melted rock.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "474d1098-0b7b-4346-952e-4341c9395623",
