                    {
                        "id": "b08fe70b-fabf-4b0d-bea7-a3621ea3f944",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-12",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The next step in the formation of sedimentary rocks after a layer of sediment is deposited on the ocean floor is:\n\nB) burying\n\nHere's the step-by-step reasoning:\n\n1. Sediments are deposited on the ocean floor through processes such as erosion and weathering of rocks on land, as well as the accumulation of organic material and minerals from the water column.\n\n2. Over time, more and more layers of sediment accumulate on top of each other. This process is called burial or deposition. As the layers of sediment build up, the pressure on the lower layers increases.\n\n3. The increased pressure from the overlying layers of sediment causes the sediments to compact and the water within the sediments to be squeezed out. This process is called compaction.\n\n4. As compaction continues, the sediments become more tightly packed, and the individual grains of sediment begin to stick together. This process is called cementation.\n\n5. Over long periods of time, the compacted and cemented sediments eventually form sedimentary rocks.\n\nSo, the correct answer is B) burying, as it is the next step after sediment deposition in the formation of sedimentary rocks.",
                        "answers": [
