                    {
                        "id": "11c9cbb0-161d-4dd8-92b0-0d62455e0f53",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-13",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Question: What is the subsequent step in the formation of sedimentary rocks after a layer of sediment has been deposited on the ocean floor?\nOptions:\nA) heating\nB) burying\nC) eroding\nD) weathering\n\nStep 1: Understand the process of sedimentary rock formation\nSedimentary rocks are formed from the accumulation and cementation of mineral and organic particles. The process involves several steps, including deposition, burial, compaction, and cementation.\n\nStep 2: Identify the current step in the process\nThe question states that a layer of sediment has been deposited on the ocean floor. This means we are at the deposition stage of the process.\n\nStep 3: Determine the next step in the process\nAfter deposition, the next step in the formation of sedimentary rocks is the burial of the sediments. This occurs when more layers of sediment are deposited on top of the existing layer, causing it to be buried deeper beneath the surface.\n\nStep 4: Match the next step with the given options\nThe next step, burying, corresponds to option B.\n\nAnswer: B) burying",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "cc15414a-21ed-4c67-a7d8-dff79f0fcfb3",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
