                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nThe correct answer is B) burying.\n\nThe formation of sedimentary rocks begins with the deposition of sediment on the ocean floor. This sediment can be composed of a variety of materials, such as sand, silt, clay, and organic matter. Once the sediment is deposited, it is then buried by additional layers of sediment. This burial process compacts the sediment and can cause chemical changes to occur, such as the formation of cementing agents. Once the sediment is buried, it can then be subjected to further processes such as heating, eroding, and weathering, which can further alter the sediment and lead to the formation of sedimentary rocks.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "49eff868-9174-4e1d-8831-39f6cdae24a7",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
