                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStudent: Which of the following is most likely an adaptation that resulted from habitat destruction?\n\nProfessor: Well, let's think about this. What is habitat destruction?\n\nStudent: It's when humans destroy an animal's natural habitat.\n\nProfessor: That's right. So, when we destroy an animal's habitat, that means they have to adapt to a new environment.\n\nStudent: Okay.\n\nProfessor: So, which of the following options do you think would be an adaptation to a new environment?\n\nStudent: I'm not sure.\n\nProfessor: Well, let's think about it. What does a water tower have to do with a bird's natural habitat?\n\nStudent: I don't know.\n\nProfessor: Well, a water tower is likely to be found in an urban environment, and that's not a natural habitat for a bird.\n\nStudent: Okay.\n\nProfessor: What about a rabbit's fur turning white in the winter?\n\nStudent: I don't know.\n\nProfessor: Well, a rabbit's natural habitat is in the woods, and in the winter, the woods are likely to be covered in snow. So, a rabbit's fur turning white would help it blend in with its surroundings and avoid being seen by predators.\n\nStudent: Okay.\n\nProfessor: What about a lizard shedding its skin?\n\nStudent: I don't know.\n\nProfessor: Well, a lizard's skin is likely to dry out in a new environment, so shedding its skin would help it stay healthy.\n\nStudent: Okay.\n\nProfessor: What about a salmon swimming upstream?\n\nStudent: I don't know.\n\nProfessor: Well, a salmon's natural habitat is in a river, and if the river is dammed, the salmon might have to swim upstream to reach its spawning grounds.\n\nStudent: Okay.\n\nProfessor: So, which of the following is most likely an adaptation that resulted from habitat destruction?\n\nStudent: I think it's the salmon swimming upstream.\n\nProfessor: That's right. When we dam a river, it can block the salmon's migration route and force them to swim upstream.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "7e57728e-0f38-49bf-a95d-7fa3ba93a126",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
