                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe Permian period was a time of great change for Earth's climate, and evidence suggests that there was extensive glaciation during this time. This could have had a major impact on ocean ecosystems, as it would have caused a steep drop in ocean salinity and density. This would have made it difficult for marine life to survive, as they would have been unable to adapt to the changes in their environment.",
