                    {
                        "id": "a6968feb-dbb3-4911-bd6c-72545e518f6c",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-12",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To answer this question, we need to consider the properties of cold air and how it behaves in relation to pressure and density.\n\nCold air is denser than warm air. This is because the molecules in cold air are more closely packed together, making it heavier and denser. Therefore, option C) is incorrect, as cold air is considered to be more dense than warmer air.\n\nOption D) is also incorrect, as cold air still contains oxygen atoms. The composition of air does not change significantly with temperature, so there will still be oxygen atoms present in cold air.\n\nNow let's consider the relationship between air pressure and the movement of air. Air flows from areas of high pressure to areas of low pressure. This is because the air molecules in high-pressure areas are more densely packed together, and they naturally move towards areas where there is more space (low-pressure areas).\n\nIn the context of mountains and valleys, cold air at the tops of mountains is denser and heavier than the warmer air in the valleys. This causes the air pressure at the tops of mountains to be higher than the air pressure in the valleys. As a result, the cold air will flow from the high-pressure area at the top of the mountain towards the low-pressure area in the valley.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is:\nA) will flow toward areas of lower pressure in valleys.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "40162410-a063-4e69-8d80-c2443f8523aa",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "A) will flow toward areas of lower pressure in valleys.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
                        "author": "thoughtsource",
                        "date": "2023/04/13 07:21:45",
                        "api_service": "openai_chat",
                        "model": "{'name': 'gpt-4', 'temperature': 0, 'max_tokens': 512}",
