                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nStep 1: Understand the definition of each of the four terms.\n\nWeathering: The process of breaking down rocks and other materials at the Earth's surface due to the action of wind, water, and other natural forces.\n\nDeposition: The process of sediment being laid down in a new location.\n\nFaulting: The process of rocks breaking and shifting due to tectonic forces.\n\nErosion: The process of wearing away of the Earth's surface by wind, water, and other natural forces.\n\nStep 2: Compare the definition of each term to the given scenario.\n\nThe freezing and expanding of water in the cracks of rocks is a form of weathering because it is the process of breaking down rocks due to the action of water.\n\nAnswer: A) Weathering.",
