                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nAnswer: A) Weathering\n\nExplanation: Weathering is the process of breaking down rocks and other materials at the Earth's surface due to the effects of wind, water, and temperature. The freezing and expanding of water in the cracks of rocks is a form of weathering because the water expands when it freezes, which causes the rocks to crack and break down. This process is known as frost wedging. Deposition is the process of sediment being deposited by water, wind, or ice. Faulting is the process of rocks being broken and shifted due to tectonic forces. Erosion is the process of rocks and other materials being worn away by wind, water, and ice.",
