                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nComplementary Knowledge: Weathering is the process of breaking down rocks and other materials at the Earth's surface due to physical, chemical, and biological processes. Deposition is the process of laying down sediment, such as sand, mud, and gravel, in a new location. Faulting is the process of fracturing rocks along a fault line, which can cause earthquakes. Erosion is the process of wearing away rocks and other materials at the Earth's surface due to physical processes, such as water, wind, and ice.\n\nSub-Questions:\n1. Does the process involve breaking down rocks?\n2. Does the process involve laying down sediment?\n3. Does the process involve fracturing rocks?\n4. Does the process involve wearing away rocks?\n\nAnswers:\n1. No\n2. No\n3. No\n4. Yes\n\nAnswer: D) Erosion",
                        "answers": [
