                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To determine which weather event is most likely to cause a forest fire, let's examine each option individually:\n\nA) A flash flood involves a large amount of water suddenly flooding an area. This would not cause a forest fire, as water typically extinguishes fires.\n\nB) A lightning strike involves a powerful electrical discharge from the atmosphere, which can generate intense heat. This heat can ignite dry vegetation and start a forest fire.\n\nC) A tornado is a rapidly rotating column of air that can cause widespread destruction. While it can uproot trees and cause damage, it is not known for starting fires.\n\nD) A hailstorm involves the formation of ice pellets that fall from the sky. These ice pellets are not capable of starting a fire.\n\nBased on this analysis, the weather event most likely to cause a forest fire is:\n\nB) a lightning strike",
