                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nThe most likely weather event to cause a forest fire is a lightning strike (B). Lightning is a common cause of forest fires because it can ignite dry vegetation and create a spark that can spread quickly in windy conditions. Flash floods (A) can cause damage to forests, but they are not likely to cause a fire. Tornadoes (C) can cause damage to forests, but they are not likely to cause a fire. Hailstorms (D) can cause damage to forests, but they are not likely to cause a fire.",
                        "answers": [
