                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To determine which alternative energy resources use gravitational energy to make electricity, let's first understand what gravitational energy is. Gravitational energy is the potential energy an object possesses due to its position in a gravitational field, such as Earth's gravity.\n\nNow let's analyze each option:\n\nA) Tidal energy and hydropower\n- Tidal energy is generated by the movement of tides, which are caused by the gravitational pull of the moon and the sun on Earth's oceans. This movement of water can be harnessed to generate electricity.\n- Hydropower is generated by the movement of water from higher elevations to lower elevations, driven by gravity. This movement of water can be harnessed to generate electricity.\n\nB) Geothermal energy and hydropower\n- Geothermal energy is generated by the heat from the Earth's core, which is not related to gravitational energy.\n- Hydropower, as explained above, uses gravitational energy.\n\nC) Wind energy and tidal energy\n- Wind energy is generated by the movement of air due to differences in air pressure, which is not directly related to gravitational energy.\n- Tidal energy, as explained above, uses gravitational energy.\n\nD) Geothermal energy and wind energy\n- Geothermal energy, as explained above, does not use gravitational energy.\n- Wind energy, as explained above, does not use gravitational energy.\n\nBased on the analysis, the correct answer is A) tidal energy and hydropower, as both of these alternative energy resources use gravitational energy to make electricity.",
