                        "cot_trigger": "zhou-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": " \n\nGravitational energy is energy that is generated by the gravitational pull of the Earth. This energy can be used to generate electricity. \n\nA) tidal energy and hydropower - Correct. Tidal energy is generated by the gravitational pull of the moon and the sun on the Earth's oceans, and hydropower is generated by the gravitational force of falling water. \n\nB) geothermal energy and hydropower - Incorrect. Geothermal energy is generated by the heat of the Earth's core, not by gravitational energy. \n\nC) wind energy and tidal energy - Incorrect. Wind energy is generated by the movement of air, not by gravitational energy. \n\nD) geothermal energy and wind energy - Incorrect. Geothermal energy is generated by the heat of the Earth's core, not by gravitational energy.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "362742b3-56fa-4687-8593-3ee1244ab5e3",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
