                        "cot_trigger": "kojima-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Gravitational energy is the energy associated with the force of gravity. It is harnessed when there is a difference in height or elevation between two points.\n\nA) Tidal energy and hydropower: Tidal energy is generated from the movement of tides, which are caused by the gravitational pull of the moon and the sun. Hydropower is generated from the movement of water from higher elevations to lower elevations, which is also influenced by gravity. So, both tidal energy and hydropower use gravitational energy to make electricity.\n\nB) Geothermal energy and hydropower: Geothermal energy is generated from the heat within the Earth, which is not related to gravitational energy. Hydropower, as mentioned earlier, uses gravitational energy. So, only hydropower uses gravitational energy in this option.\n\nC) Wind energy and tidal energy: Wind energy is generated from the movement of air, which is not directly related to gravitational energy. Tidal energy, as mentioned earlier, uses gravitational energy. So, only tidal energy uses gravitational energy in this option.\n\nD) Geothermal energy and wind energy: As mentioned earlier, both geothermal energy and wind energy do not use gravitational energy to make electricity.\n\nBased on the analysis, the correct answer is A) tidal energy and hydropower.",
