                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nWhen light hits a mirror, it is not refracted because refraction occurs when light passes through a medium with a different density, such as from air to water or from air to glass. In the case of a mirror, the light is not passing through any medium, so there is no refraction.\n\nInstead, the light is reflected off the mirror's surface. This means that the answer is B) reflected. Some of the light may be absorbed by the mirror's surface, but most of it is reflected back towards the source. There is no transmission of light through the mirror, as it is a solid object that does not allow light to pass through.",
