                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nB) Reflected.\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n\n1. When light hits a surface, it can either be absorbed, transmitted, refracted, or reflected.\n2. Refraction occurs when light passes through a medium and changes direction due to a change in its speed.\n3. Transmission occurs when light passes through a medium without being absorbed or reflected.\n4. Absorption occurs when light is absorbed by the material it hits, converting the light energy into heat or other forms of energy.\n5. Reflection occurs when light bounces off a surface and changes direction without being absorbed or transmitted.\n6. When light hits a mirror, it is reflected back in the same direction, making it the correct answer.",
