                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "When light hits a mirror, most of the light is reflected. This is because mirrors are designed to have a smooth surface that allows light to bounce off of it at the same angle it hit the surface. This reflection creates an image of the object that is being reflected. Refraction occurs when light passes through a medium with a different density, such as when light passes through a prism. Absorption occurs when light is absorbed by an object, causing it to appear a certain color. Transmission occurs when light passes through a medium without being absorbed or reflected, such as when light passes through a clear glass window. Therefore, the correct answer is B) reflected.",
