                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Rephrased question: What property is greater for the second sound wave produced by a flute, which has the same pitch as the first but is louder?\n\nStep-by-step solution:\n- The pitch of the two sound waves is the same, so their frequency must be the same. Eliminate option A.\n- The loudness of a sound wave is determined by its amplitude, which is the height of the wave. Therefore, the second sound wave must have a greater amplitude than the first. Option B is the correct answer.\n- Wavelength is the distance between two consecutive peaks or troughs of a wave. It is not related to the loudness of the sound wave. Eliminate option C.\n- The speed of sound in air is constant, so it is not affected by the loudness of the sound wave. Eliminate option D.\n\nAnswer: B) Amplitude",
