                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nAnswer: B) Amplitude\n\nExplanation: Frequency is the number of sound waves produced per second, and is the same for both sound waves. Wavelength is the distance between two successive wave crests, and is also the same for both sound waves. Speed in air is the speed at which sound waves travel, and is also the same for both sound waves. Therefore, the only property that is greater for the second sound wave is amplitude, which is the loudness of the sound wave.",
