                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: The special parts in plant cells that capture sunlight are called chloroplasts. Chloroplasts contain chlorophyll, which is the pigment that absorbs sunlight and allows photosynthesis to occur.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What are chloroplasts and what is their function?\n2. In which part of the plant do chloroplasts typically exist?\n3. Which part of the plant is responsible for photosynthesis?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Chloroplasts are special organelles found in plant cells that contain chlorophyll and are responsible for photosynthesis, the process by which plants convert sunlight into energy.\n2. Chloroplasts are typically found in the leaves of plants, although they can also be found in other parts of the plant such as stems and flowers.\n3. The leaves of a plant are primarily responsible for photosynthesis, as they contain the most chloroplasts and are the main site of photosynthesis in most plants.\n\nConclusion:\nBased on the sub-questions and answers, we can conclude that the part of the plant where you will find the most chloroplasts (and therefore the most parts that capture sunlight) is the leaves. Therefore, the answer to the original question is C) leaves.",
